title: Social welfare policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: social_welfare_timer = 10; month_actions += 1
view-if: dvp_in_government and (economic_minister_party == dvp_name or finance_minister_party == dvp_name) and social_welfare_timer = 0
card-image: img/portraits/ThielOtto.jpg

= Social Welfare Policy

The Republic maintains an extensive social welfare program, including unemployment insurance, healthcare, and old age care, primarily the work of the <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**SPD**</span>. [? if (labor_strength + democratic_strength + progressive_strength) >= (liberal_strength + industrialist_strength + nationalist_strength + peoples_conservative_strength): Our party’s position has moved steadily towards maintaining, or even increasing welfare spending. ?][? if (labor_strength + democratic_strength + progressive_strength) < (liberal_strength + industrialist_strength + nationalist_strength + peoples_conservative_strength): Our party supports dismantling or at least reforming the welfare system. ?]

- @reduce_spending: Reduce spending on welfare.
- @increase_spending_pre_depression: Increase spending on welfare.
- @increase_spending_post_depression: Increase spending (welfare levels will remain about the same).
- @spending_same_pre_depression: Keep spending the same.
- @spending_same_post_depression: Keep spending the same (effectively a service cut).
- @easy_discard
#- @cancel_advisor_action

@reduce_spending
subtitle: This will hurt our small labor wing. +1 Budget
unavailable-subtitle: There is nothing left to cut.
choose-if: welfare >= -5
on-arrival: budget += 1; workers_dvp -= 6; unemployed_dvp -= 6; workers_kpd += 3; welfare -= 1; industrialist_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent += 5; progressive_dissent += 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if spd_in_government; spd_patience -= 25 if spd_toleration; spd_relation -= 3; spd_left += 1; pro_republic -= 3; demand_for_action_countdown += 6; inflation -= 0.3; unemployed += 0.4; economic_growth -= 0.2;

We have reduced levels of social welfare spending. This means more poverty and suffering for the working class.


@increase_spending_pre_depression
view-if: unemployed <= 15
choose-if: budget > 0
subtitle: -1 Budget
on-arrival: budget -= 1; workers_dvp += 4*(1-dissent); unemployed_dvp += 3*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 3 if (spd_toleration or spd_in_government); unemployed_spd += 2 if (spd_toleration or spd_in_government); welfare += 1; industrialist_dissent += 5; labor_dissent -= 5; labor_strength += 5; progressive_dissent -= 5; progressive_strength += 3; spd_patience += 25 if spd_toleration; spd_relation += 3; spd_left -= 1; demand_for_action_countdown -= 2; inflation += 0.3; unemployed -= 0.4; economic_growth += 0.2;

We have increased welfare spending. The workers and our labor wing are pleased.

@increase_spending_post_depression
view-if: unemployed > 15
choose-if: budget > 0
on-arrival: budget -= 1; workers_dvp += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_dvp += 3*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 2 if (spd_toleration or spd_in_government); unemployed_spd += 1 if (spd_toleration or spd_in_government); demand_for_action_countdown -= 2; inflation += 0.3; industrialist_dissent += 5; labor_dissent -= 5; labor_strength += 5; progressive_dissent -= 5; progressive_strength += 3; spd_patience += 25 if spd_toleration; spd_relation += 3; spd_left -= 1;
subtitle: The increased levels of unemployment necessitate more spending on aid to maintain the same benefits. -1 Budget

Increasing welfare spending is necessary in light of the rise in unemployment, so we are essentially treading water.


@spending_same_pre_depression
view-if: unemployed <= 15

We have kept welfare spending the same.

@spending_same_post_depression
view-if: unemployed > 15
on-arrival: workers_dvp -= 3; unemployed_dvp -= 4; welfare -= 1;
subtitle: The increased levels of unemployment necessitate more spending on aid.

Increasing welfare spending is necessary in light of the rise in unemployment, so we have essentially cut welfare. The workers are justifiably displeased - we are sacrificing their livelihoods for austerity.
